# Commercial S3.1 allowlist target-hash diagnosis

Date: 2026-08-29

The first execution of the hash-bound allowlist repair stopped before the live
file exchange with `ALLOWLIST_TRANSFORM_DRIFT`. The configured target digest
had been calculated from a different serialization assumption. The controller
removed its temporary file on exit; the live allowlist retained its exact old
SHA-256, no repair evidence was created, and the service remained inactive
with zero restarts.

A read-only server calculation, without outputting private Telegram IDs,
confirmed exactly one legacy creator occurrence and one binding. Replacing
only the equal-length creator UUID in the original bytes produces SHA-256
`12b5c220c309128fd5607d75bbc066c69721d5e373b8f1e57fe4c108db7a222f`.
This is the required target because it preserves every other byte, including
private IDs, roles and formatting. Control, gate and tests bind this corrected
digest before any retry.
